---
import { testimonial } from "../data/site";
import VerifiedBadge from "./icons/VerifiedBadge.astro";
import XLogo from "./icons/XLogo.astro";
---

<div class="max-w-xl">
  <a
    href={testimonial.url}
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    class="group block border border-white/8 bg-neutral-950/80 p-5 transition-all duration-300 hover:border-white/16 hover:bg-neutral-900/80"
  >
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
      <img
        src={testimonial.avatar}
        alt={testimonial.author}
        width="40"
        height="40"
        loading="lazy"
        class="h-10 w-10 shrink-0 rounded-full object-cover"
      />
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1">
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-100">{testimonial.author}</span>
          <VerifiedBadge class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-sky-400" />
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500">{testimonial.role}</p>
      </div>
      <span
        class="ml-auto shrink-0 text-neutral-500 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:text-neutral-200"
      >
        <XLogo class="h-4 w-4" />
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm font-light leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">
      <p>
        If you are building anything consumer-centric and want someone who is a combination of 10x
        dev + can think from product POV, swoop in
        <span class="text-neutral-100">@mizanxali</span>'s DM for a chat ASAP.
      </p>
      <p>
        Worked with Mizan for over 3 years now, and I can confidently say that he is a high agency
        person, with an extreme bias for action, a straight shooter and will give you the most
        honest feedback ever.
      </p>
      <p>
        At Huddle01, he played one of the most important roles in building numerous
        consumer-centric plays, followed by SDKs and whatnot. The list goes on.
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-200">
        <span class="font-medium">TLDR:</span> Any org will be lucky to have him.
      </p>
    </div>
    <span
      class="mt-4 inline-block text-xs text-neutral-500 transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:text-neutral-200"
      >Read on X →</span
    >
  </a>
</div>
